{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790527658968,"sessionID":"ses_f1c5a4875ffeR5KO5Iu7pV8EKt","part":{"id":"prt_0e3c3c54a001U58ZKLCosI7h8R","messageID":"msg_0e3c3c1b5001CTK7pICcu3YeRl","sessionID":"ses_f1c5a4875ffeR5KO5Iu7pV8EKt","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I have a clear picture of the bot's performance. Let me analyze the deaths:\n\n- Seed 8 is a massive outlier at 0.554 - reached Dlvl:27, killed by giant eel\n- Seeds 2, 5, 12, 14 all die of starvation early (Xp:3-4)\n- Seeds 3, 9, 13 die to little monsters early (cave spider, wererat, little dog)\n- Seeds 1, 6, 11 die to monsters at Xp:5-8\n- Seeds 0, 4 die at Xp:9 (gargoyle, soldier ant)\n- Seed 7 dies to lightning at Dlvl:10\n- Seed 10 dies to owlbear at Dlvl:9\n- Seed 6 dies to dwarf zombie at Xp:5\n\nThe key problem: The bot dies very early frequently. Most seeds don't even get past Xp:10. Only seed 8 gets to Dlvl:27.\n\nLet me look at the current bot code to understand what strategies are in place and what's going wrong.\n\nThe key issues I can see:\n1. Starvation - seeds 2, 12, 14 die early\n2. Early monster deaths - seeds 3, 6, 9, 13, 11\n3. Unidentified threats - gargoyle, soldier ant, rothe, hobbit, brown mold\n4. Lightning deaths\n\nLet me look at the autoascend code to understand the current strategy.","time":{"start":1790527653194,"end":1790527658963}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790527659328,"sessionID":"ses_f1c5a4875ffeR5KO5Iu7pV8EKt","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call-a297aad4-0834-4e60-a597-85ec8fda047c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/autoascend/global_logic.py"},"output":"<path>/workspace/autoascend/global_logic.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: from enum import IntEnum, auto\n2: \n3: import nle.nethack as nh\n4: import numpy as np\n5: from nle.nethack import actions as A\n6: \n7: from . import objects as O\n8: from . import soko_solver\n9: from . import utils\n10: from .character import Character\n11: from .exceptions import AgentPanic\n12: from .glyph import Hunger, G, MON\n13: from .item import Item, flatten_items\n14: from .item.item_priority_base import ItemPriorityBase\n15: from .level import Level\n16: from .strategy import Strategy\n17: \n18: \n19: class ItemPriority(ItemPriorityBase):\n20:     MAX_NUMBER_OF_ITEMS = 26 * 2 - 1  # + coin slot, one slot should be left for item arranging\n21:     def __init__(self, agent):\n22:         self.agent = agent\n23:         self._take_sacrificial_corpses = False\n24:         self._drop_gold_till_turn = -float('inf')\n25: \n26:     def _split(self, items, forced_items, weight_capacity):\n27:         if self.agent.global_logic.squeeze_cap:\n28:             weight_capacity = min(weight_capacity, SQUEEZE_WEIGHT_CAP)\n29:         remaining_weight = weight_capacity\n30:         ret_inv = {}\n31:         for item in forced_items:\n32:             remaining_weight -= item.weight()\n33:             ret_inv[item] = item.count\n34: \n35:         ret_bag = {}\n36:         bag = None\n37: \n38:         def add_item(item, count=None, to_bag=False):\n39:             nonlocal ret_inv, ret_bag, remaining_weight\n40:             assert isinstance(item, Item)\n41:             if to_bag and bag is not None and item is not bag:\n42:                 ret = ret_bag\n43:             else:\n44:                 ret = ret_inv\n45: \n46:             if remaining_weight < 0 or \\\n47:                     (ret is ret_inv and len(ret) >= ItemPriority.MAX_NUMBER_OF_ITEMS):  # TODO: coin slot\n48:                 return\n49: \n50:             how_many_already_total = ret_inv.get(item, 0) + ret_bag.get(item, 0)\n51:             how_many_already = ret.get(item, 0)\n52:             unit_weight = item.unit_weight(with_content=False)\n53:             # weightless items (e.g. wraith corpses) would make this an infinite count\n54:             max_to_add = item.count if unit_weight <= 0 else int(remaining_weight // unit_weight)\n55:             if count is not None:\n56:                 max_to_add = min(max_to_add, count)\n57:             ret[item] = min(item.count, how_many_already_total + max_to_add) - (how_many_already_total - how_many_already)\n58:             remaining_weight -= item.unit_weight(with_content=False) * (ret[item] - how_many_already)\n59: \n60:         for item in items:\n61:             if item.is_container() and item.status in [Item.UNCURSED, Item.BLESSED] and item.objs[0].desc == 'bag':\n62:                 bag = item  # TODO: select the best\n63:                 add_item(bag)\n64: \n65:         if self._drop_gold_till_turn < self.agent.blstats.time:\n66:             for item in items:\n67:                 if item.category == nh.COIN_CLASS:\n68:                     add_item(item)\n69: \n70:         def add_pick():\n71:             for item in items:\n72:                 if item.is_unambiguous() and item.objs[0].name in ('pick-axe', 'dwarvish mattock') and \\\n73:                         item.status != Item.CURSED:\n74:                     add_item(item)\n75:                     break\n76: \n77:         # squeezing through is only needed to get the pick back to the main dungeon, so under the\n78:         # squeeze cap it goes first\n79:         if self.agent.global_logic.squeeze_cap:\n80:             add_pick()\n81: \n82:         for allow_unknown_status in [False, True]:\n83:             item = self.agent.inventory.get_best_melee_weapon(items=forced_items + items,\n84:                                                               allow_unknown_status=allow_unknown_status)\n85:             if item is not None:\n86:                 add_item(item)\n87: \n88:             for item in self.agent.inventory.get_best_armorset(items=forced_items + items,\n89:                                                                allow_unknown_status=allow_unknown_status):\n90:                 if item is not None:\n91:                     add_item(item)\n92: \n93:         # a digging tool turns the rest of the game into a dive (Agent.dig_down), worth far more than\n94:         # anything else we could carry in its weight\n95:         add_pick()\n96: \n97:         for item in items:\n98:             if item.is_unambiguous():\n99:                 if item.object in [\n100:                         O.from_name('healing', nh.POTION_CLASS),\n101:                         O.from_name('extra healing', nh.POTION_CLASS),\n102:                         O.from_name('full healing', nh.POTION_CLASS)]:\n103:                     add_item(item)\n104: \n105:                 if self.agent.character.role in [Character.RANGER, Character.ROGUE,\n106:                                                  Character.SAMURAI, Character.TOURIST] and \\\n107:                         (item.is_launcher() or item.is_fired_projectile()):\n108:                     add_item(item)\n109: \n110:         if self.agent.character.alignment == Character.LAWFUL:\n111:             for item in sorted(filter(lambda i: i.objs[0].name == 'long sword', items),\n112:                                key=lambda i: -utils.calc_dps(*self.agent.character.get_melee_bonus(i))):\n113:                 add_item(item)\n114:                 break\n115: \n116:         for item in sorted(filter(lambda i: i.is_thrown_projectile(), items),\n117:                            key=lambda i: -utils.calc_dps(*self.agent.character.get_ranged_bonus(None, i))):\n118:             add_item(item)\n119: \n120:         for item in sorted(filter(lambda i: i.is_food() and not i.is_corpse(), items),\n121:                            key=lambda x: -x.nutrition_per_weight() - 1000 * (x.objs[0].name == 'sprig of wolfsbane')):\n122:             add_item(item)\n123: \n124:         if self._take_sacrificial_corpses:\n125:             for item in filter(self.agent.global_logic.can_sacrify, items):\n126:                 add_item(item)\n127: \n128:         # TODO: take nh.COIN_CLASS once shopping is implemented.\n129:         # You have to drop all coins not to be attacked by a vault guard\n130: \n131:         for item in sorted(items, key=lambda i: i.unit_weight(with_content=False)):\n132:             if item.category in [nh.POTION_CLASS, nh.RING_CLASS, nh.AMULET_CLASS, nh.WAND_CLASS, nh.SCROLL_CLASS, nh.TOOL_CLASS]:\n133:                 if (not isinstance(item.objs[0], O.Container) or not item.is_chest()) and \\\n134:                         not item.is_possible_container():\n135:                     to_bag = O.from_name('cancellation', nh.WAND_CLASS) not in item.objs and \\\n136:                              not item.is_offensive_usable_wand()\n137:                     to_bag = False\n138:                     if not item.is_container():  # remove condition to pick up bags\n139:                         add_item(item, to_bag=to_bag)\n140: \n141:         categories = [nh.WEAPON_CLASS, nh.ARMOR_CLASS, nh.TOOL_CLASS, nh.FOOD_CLASS, nh.GEM_CLASS, nh.AMULET_CLASS,\n142:                       nh.RING_CLASS, nh.POTION_CLASS, nh.SCROLL_CLASS, nh.SPBOOK_CLASS, nh.WAND_CLASS]\n143:         for item in sorted(items, key=lambda i: i.unit_weight(with_content=False)):\n144:             if item.category in categories and not isinstance(item.objs[0], O.Container) and not item.is_corpse():\n145:                 if item.status == Item.UNKNOWN:\n146:                     to_bag = O.from_name('cancellation', nh.WAND_CLASS) not in item.objs and \\\n147:                              not item.is_offensive_usable_wand()\n148:                     to_bag = False\n149:                     if not item.is_container():  # remove condition to pick up bags\n150:                         add_item(item, to_bag=to_bag)\n151: \n152:         r = {None: [ret_inv.get(item, 0) for item in items]}\n153:         if bag is not None:\n154:             r[bag] = [ret_bag.get(item, 0) for item in items]\n155:         for item in items:\n156:             if item.is_container() and item is not bag and ret_inv.get(item, 0) != 0:\n157:                 r[item] = [0 for _ in items]\n158:         return r\n159: \n160: \n161: class Milestone(IntEnum):\n162:     BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL = auto()\n163:     FIND_GNOMISH_MINES = auto()\n164:     # FIND_LIGHT_GNOMISH_MINES = auto()\n165:     # FARM_LIGHT_GNOMISH_MINES = auto()\n166:     FIND_MINETOWN = auto()\n167:     FIND_SOKOBAN = auto()\n168:     SOLVE_SOKOBAN = auto()\n169:     FIND_MINES_END = auto()\n170:     GO_DOWN = auto() # TODO\n171: \n172: \n173: # experience level from which a character carrying a pick-axe skips the Dlvl 1 grind and digs down\n174: EARLY_DIG_XL = 3\n175: # turns a non-gnome, non-dwarf spends hunting the Mines' dwarves for a pick-axe after the Dlvl 1\n176: # grind before it gives up and dives by the stairs; 0 disables the hunt\n177: PICK_HUNT_TURNS = 3000\n178: # roles whose pick hunt paid off when doubled (73-identity A/B)\n179: ROLE_PICK_HUNT_TURNS = {}\n180: # NetHack refuses a diagonal squeeze between two rock squares to anyone carrying more than 600\n181: SQUEEZE_WEIGHT_LIMIT = 600\n182: # the inventory budget once squeezing is needed, a little under the limit for weight misestimates\n183: SQUEEZE_WEIGHT_CAP = 580\n184: # experience level the Dlvl 1 grind stops at before the deep phase begins\n185: GRIND_XL = 8\n186: # gnomes and dwarves walk the peaceful Mines to Mines' End before diving the main dungeon\n187: MINES_FOLK_ROUTE = True\n188: # Per-role overrides picked from a 73-identity A/B on the public seeds (Xp 5 vs Xp 8 grind,\n189: # with and without the Mines routes): fighters and fragile casters both do better grinding\n190: # to Xp 8 first; Rogues and Samurai dive the main dungeon without the Mines detours.\n191: # A later sweep over Xp 5/6/7/8 moved Knights and Valkyries to 7 and Healers to 6.\n192: ROLE_GRIND_XL = {}\n193: # Xp from which a character carrying a pick digs down, where it differs from EARLY_DIG_XL\n194: # (a Monk-only Xp 8 dig, as in github.com/eL1fe/nethacker@ff8e491, measured worse here)\n195: ROLE_EARLY_DIG_XL = {}\n196: # ablation switches for fixes made while diving (see their call sites)\n197: DIVE_SKIPS_EXPLORATION = True\n198: LEAVE_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY = False\n199: # Roles for which leaving the Dlvl 1 grind when out of food pays (73-identity A/B): the others\n200: # (Healers, Knights, Priests, Rogues, Tourists, Valkyries) do better finishing the grind.\n201: ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY = {Character.ARCHEOLOGIST, Character.BARBARIAN, Character.CAVEMAN,\n202:                                    Character.RANGER, Character.SAMURAI, Character.MONK,\n203:                                    Character.WIZARD}\n204: \n205: \n206: def early_dig_xl(character):\n207:     return ROLE_EARLY_DIG_XL.get(character.role, EARLY_DIG_XL)\n208: \n209: ROLES_WITHOUT_MINES_ROUTES = {Character.ROGUE, Character.SAMURAI}\n210: \n211: \n212: class GlobalLogic:\n213:     def __init__(self, agent):\n214:         self.agent = agent\n215:         self.milestone = Milestone(1)\n216:         self._pick_hunt_start = None  # turn the Mines pick hunt began, if it did\n217:         self.step_completion_log = {}  # Milestone -> (step, turn)\n218: \n219:         self.item_priority = ItemPriority(self.agent)\n220: \n221:         self.oracle_level = None\n222:         self.minetown_level = None\n223: \n224:         self._got_artifact = False\n225: \n226:         self.squeeze_cap = False  # carry at most SQUEEZE_WEIGHT_CAP (see _update_squeeze_cap)\n227:         self._squeeze_hits = 0\n228:         self._squeeze_check_turn = -float('inf')\n229: \n230:     def _grind_xl(self):\n231:         return ROLE_GRIND_XL.get(self.agent.character.role, GRIND_XL)\n232: \n233:     def _role_routes(self):\n234:         return self.agent.character.role not in ROLES_WITHOUT_MINES_ROUTES\n235: \n236:     def _update_squeeze_cap(self):\n237:         # hypothesis: a pick hunter that wins its digging tool in the Gnomish Mines often never turns\n238:         # it into a dive, stalling on a Mines level for 5k-20k turns and scoring only its Xp\n239:         # (~0.05-0.18) instead of the Dlvl 10-26 dive (0.13-0.5). Three things hold it there:\n240:         # 1. the bot fills its pack to its carrying capacity (usually 700-1000, and the pick adds\n241:         #    100-120), but NetHack forbids squeezing diagonally between two rock squares to anyone\n242:         #    carrying over 600, and the Mines' cave levels are full of such gaps, so the up stairs\n243:         #    are often unreachable. When a staircase of a Mines level stays reachable only by\n244:         #    squeezing, cap the pack below the limit (the pick first) for the rest of the Mines\n245:         #    visit, so the bot drops its least valued items and walks on (this method);\n246:         # 2. before heading for the stairs it first explores every corner of each item-strewn Mines\n247:         #    level, which with the fights and pickups along the way takes thousands of turns\n248:         #    (_leaving_mines_to_dig);\n249:         # 3. a dwarvish mattock is two-handed and cannot be applied under a shield, so a hunter\n250:         #    whose tool is a mattock tries to dig and fails on every square\n251:         #    (Inventory.get_best_armorset, Agent.pick_for_digging).\n252:         # Outside the Mines and without a digging tool nothing changes.\n253:         level = self.agent.current_level()\n254:         if level.dungeon_number != Level.GNOMISH_MINES:\n255:             self.squeeze_cap = False\n256:             self._squeeze_hits = 0\n257:             return\n258:         if self.squeeze_cap or self.agent.inventory.items.total_weight <= SQUEEZE_WEIGHT_LIMIT:\n259:             return\n260:         turn = self.agent.blstats.time\n261:         if turn - self._squeeze_check_turn < 10:\n262:             return\n263:         self._squeeze_check_turn = turn\n264:         only_squeezing = (self.agent.bfs(can_squeeze=True) != -1) & (self.agent.bfs(can_squeeze=False) == -1)\n265:         # a monster standing in a gap looks the same, and exploring may still turn up another way\n266:         # around, so the cut-off has to persist for a while\n267:         if (only_squeezing & utils.isin(level.objects, G.STAIR_UP, G.STAIR_DOWN)).any():\n268:             self._squeeze_hits += 1\n269:         else:\n270:             self._squeeze_hits = 0\n271:         if self._squeeze_hits >= 50:\n272:             self.squeeze_cap = True\n273: \n274:     def _leaving_mines_to_dig(self):\n275:         # (see _update_squeeze_cap) with the digging tool in hand the Mines level has nothing left\n276:         # to offer: walk straight back to the main dungeon rather than first exploring every corner\n277:         # of this item-strewn cave level, which with fights and pickups can take thousands of turns\n278:         return self.milestone == Milestone.GO_DOWN and \\\n279:                self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES and \\\n280:                self.agent.pick_for_digging() is not None\n281: \n282:     def update(self):\n283:         self._update_squeeze_cap()\n284:         if not self.agent.character.prop.hallu:\n285:             if utils.isin(self.agent.glyphs, G.ORACLE).any():\n286:                 if self.oracle_level is None:\n287:                     self.oracle_level = self.agent.current_level().key()\n288:                 else:\n289:                     assert self.oracle_level == self.agent.current_level().key()\n290: \n291:             if self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES and \\\n292:                     utils.isin(self.agent.glyphs, G.SHOPKEEPER).any():\n293:                 if self.minetown_level is None:\n294:                     self.minetown_level = self.agent.current_level().key()\n295:                 else:\n296:                     assert self.minetown_level == self.agent.current_level().key()\n297: \n298:     @utils.debug_log('solving sokoban')\n299:     @Strategy.wrap\n300:     def solve_sokoban_strategy(self):\n301:         # TODO: refactor\n302:         if not utils.isin(self.agent.current_level().objects, G.TRAPS).any():\n303:             yield False\n304:         yield True\n305: \n306:         def push_bolder(ty, tx, dy, dx):\n307:             while 1:\n308:                 if self.agent.bfs()[ty, tx] == -1:\n309:                     return False\n310:                 self.agent.go_to(ty, tx, debug_tiles_args=dict(color=(255, 255, 255), is_path=True))\n311:                 with self.agent.atom_operation():\n312:                     direction = self.agent.calc_direction(ty, tx, ty + dy, tx + dx)\n313:                     self.agent.direction(direction)\n314:                     message = self.agent.message\n315: \n316:                 if (self.agent.blstats.y, self.agent.blstats.x) == (ty, tx):\n317:                     assert 'You hear a monster behind the boulder.' in message or \\\n318:                            'You try to move the boulder, but in vain.' in message, message\n319:                     if self.agent.bfs()[ty + dy, tx + dx] != -1:\n320:                         self.agent.go_to(ty + dy, tx + dx, debug_tiles_args=dict(color=(255, 255, 255), is_path=True))\n321:                         continue\n322:                     else:\n323:                         pickaxe = None\n324:                         for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items):\n325:                             if item.is_unambiguous() and \\\n326:                                     item.object in [O.from_name('pick-axe'), O.from_name('dwarvish mattock')]:\n327:                                 pickaxe = item\n328:                                 break\n329:                         if pickaxe is not None:\n330:                             with self.agent.atom_operation():\n331:                                 pickaxe = self.agent.inventory.move_to_inventory(pickaxe)\n332:                                 self.agent.step(A.Command.APPLY)\n333:                                 self.agent.type_text(self.agent.inventory.items.get_letter(pickaxe))\n334:                                 self.agent.direction(direction)\n335:                             return True\n336:                 else:\n337:                     return True\n338: \n339:                 # TODO: not sure what to do\n340:                 self.agent.exploration.explore1(None).run()\n341: \n342:         while 1:\n343:             wall_map = utils.isin(self.agent.current_level().objects, G.WALL)\n344:             for smap, answer in soko_solver.maps.items():\n345:                 sokomap = soko_solver.convert_map(smap)\n346:                 offset = np.array(min(zip(*wall_map.nonzero()))) - \\\n347:                          np.array(min(zip(*(sokomap.sokomap == soko_solver.WALL).nonzero())))\n348:                 mask = wall_map[offset[0] : offset[0] + sokomap.sokomap.shape[0],\n349:                                 offset[1] : offset[1] + sokomap.sokomap.shape[1]]\n350:                 if (mask & (sokomap.sokomap == soko_solver.WALL) == mask).all():\n351:                     break\n352:             else:\n353:                 assert 0, 'sokomap not found'\n354: \n355:             def simulate_move(y, x, dy, dx):\n356:                 # the real level diverged from the solver (a boulder got destroyed,\n357:                 # displaced or buried), so the stored solution no longer applies\n358:                 try:\n359:                     sokomap.move(y, x, dy, dx)\n360:                 except AssertionError:\n361:                     self.agent.stats_logger.log_event('sokoban_dropped')\n362:                     self.milestone = Milestone(int(self.milestone) + 1)\n363:                     raise AgentPanic('sokomap desynced')\n364: \n365:             possible_mimics = set()\n366:             last_resort_move = None\n367:             for (y, x), (dy, dx) in answer:\n368:                 boulder_map = utils.isin(self.agent.glyphs, G.BOULDER)\n369:                 mask = boulder_map[offset[0] : offset[0] + sokomap.sokomap.shape[0],\n370:                                    offset[1] : offset[1] + sokomap.sokomap.shape[1]]\n371:                 ty, tx = offset[0] + y - dy, offset[1] + x - dx,\n372:                 soko_boulder_mask = sokomap.sokomap == soko_solver.BOULDER\n373:                 if self.agent.bfs()[ty, tx] != -1 and \\\n374:                         ((soko_boulder_mask | mask) == soko_boulder_mask).all() and \\\n375:                         self.agent.glyphs[ty + dy, tx + dx] in G.BOULDER:\n376: \n377:                     soko_dis1 = sokomap.bfs()\n378:                     simulate_move(y, x, dy, dx)\n379:                     soko_dis2 = sokomap.bfs()\n380: \n381:                     # see points that will no longer be accessible\n382:                     with self.agent.env.debug_log('checking for monsters'):\n383:                         to_visit_mask = self.agent.bfs() != -1\n384:                         to_visit_mask[offset[0] : offset[0] + sokomap.sokomap.shape[0],\n385:                                       offset[1] : offset[1] + sokomap.sokomap.shape[1]] &= \\\n386:                                               (soko_dis1 != -1) & (soko_dis2 == -1)\n387: \n388:                         with self.agent.env.debug_tiles(to_visit_mask, color=(255, 0, 0, 128)):\n389:                             while to_visit_mask.any():\n390:                                 vy, vx = list(zip(*to_visit_mask.nonzero()))[0]\n391:                                 to_visit_mask[vy, vx] = 0\n392: \n393:                                 def clear_neighbors():\n394:                                     to_visit_mask[self.agent.blstats.y, self.agent.blstats.x] = 0\n395:                                     to_visit_mask[utils.isin(self.agent.glyphs, G.VISIBLE_FLOOR)] = 0\n396:                                     return not to_visit_mask[vy, vx]\n397: \n398:                                 self.agent.go_to(vy, vx, callback=clear_neighbors)\n399: \n400:                     if not push_bolder(ty, tx, dy, dx):\n401:                         continue\n402: \n403:                     possible_mimics = set()\n404:                     last_resort_move = None\n405: \n406:                     if not utils.isin(self.agent.current_level().objects, G.TRAPS).any():\n407:                         return\n408: \n409:                 else:\n410:                     simulate_move(y, x, dy, dx)\n411: \n412:                 if (~soko_boulder_mask | mask).all():\n413:                     if self.agent.bfs()[ty, tx] != -1 and \\\n414:                             self.agent.glyphs[ty + dy, tx + dx] in G.BOULDER and \\\n415:                             last_resort_move is None:\n416:                         last_resort_move = (ty, tx, dy, dx)\n417: \n418:                     if not possible_mimics:\n419:                         for mim_y, mim_x in zip(*(~soko_boulder_mask & mask).nonzero()):\n420:                             possible_mimics.add((mim_y + offset[0], mim_x + offset[1]))\n421: \n422: \n423:             # sokoban configuration is not in the list. Check for mimics\n424:             with self.agent.env.debug_log('mimics'):\n425:                 with self.agent.env.debug_tiles(possible_mimics, color=(255, 0, 0, 128)):\n426:                     for mim_y, mim_x in sorted(possible_mimics):\n427:                         if (self.agent.bfs()[max(0, mim_y - 1) : mim_y + 2, max(0, mim_x - 1) : mim_x + 2] != -1).any():\n428:                             self.agent.go_to(mim_y, mim_x, stop_one_before=True,\n429:                                              debug_tiles_args=dict(color=(255, 0, 0), is_path=True))\n430:                             for _ in range(3):\n431:                                 self.agent.search()\n432: \n433:             # last resort move (sometimes we can see a mimic diagonally but cannot reach it)\n434:             with self.agent.env.debug_log('last_resort'):\n435:                 if last_resort_move is not None:\n436:                     ty, tx, dy, dx = last_resort_move\n437:                     push_bolder(ty, tx, dy, dx)\n438:                     continue\n439: \n440:             self.agent.stats_logger.log_event('sokoban_dropped')\n441:             self.milestone = Milestone(int(self.milestone) + 1)\n442:             raise AgentPanic('sokomap unsolvable')\n443: \n444:     @Strategy.wrap\n445:     def wait_out_unexpected_state_strategy(self):\n446:         yielded = False\n447:         while (\n448:                 self.agent.character.prop.blind or\n449:                 self.agent.character.prop.confusion or\n450:                 self.agent.character.prop.stun or\n451:                 self.agent.character.prop.hallu or\n452:                 self.agent.character.prop.polymorph):\n453:             if not yielded:\n454:                 yield True\n455:                 yielded = True\n456: \n457:             self.agent.direction('.')\n458: \n459:         if not yielded:\n460:             yield False\n461: \n462:     @utils.debug_log('identify_items_on_altar')\n463:     @Strategy.wrap\n464:     def identify_items_on_altar(self):\n465:         mask = utils.isin(self.agent.current_level().objects, G.ALTAR)\n466:         if not mask.any():\n467:             yield False\n468: \n469:         dis = self.agent.bfs()\n470:         mask &= dis != -1\n471:         if not mask.any():\n472:             yield False\n473: \n474:         yield any((item.status == Item.UNKNOWN for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items)\n475:                    if item.can_be_dropped_from_inventory()))\n476: \n477:         (ty, tx), *_ = zip(*(mask & (dis == dis[mask].min())).nonzero())\n478:         self.agent.go_to(ty, tx)\n479:         items_to_drop = [item for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items)\n480:                          if item.can_be_dropped_from_inventory() and item.status == Item.UNKNOWN]\n481:         if not items_to_drop:\n482:             raise AgentPanic('items to drop on altar vanished')\n483: \n484:         # TODO: move chunking to inventory.drop\n485:         items_to_drop = items_to_drop[:self.agent.inventory.items.free_slots()]\n486: \n487:         self.agent.inventory.drop(items_to_drop)\n488: \n489:     @utils.debug_log('dip_for_excalibur')\n490:     @Strategy.wrap\n491:     def dip_for_excalibur(self):\n492:         if self.agent.character.alignment != Character.LAWFUL or self.agent.blstats.experience_level < 5:\n493:             yield False\n494:         if self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES and \\\n495:                 (self.minetown_level is None or self.agent.current_level().key() == self.minetown_level):\n496:             yield False\n497: \n498:         dis = self.agent.bfs()\n499:         mask = utils.isin(self.agent.current_level().objects, G.FOUNTAIN) & (dis != -1)\n500:         if not mask.any():\n501:             yield False\n502: \n503:         def excalibur_candidate():\n504:             candidate = None\n505:             for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items):\n506:                 if item.is_unambiguous() and item.object == O.from_name('long sword'):\n507:                     if item.dmg_bonus is not None: # TODO: better condition for excalibur existance\n508:                         return None\n509:                     candidate = item\n510:             return candidate\n511: \n512:         if excalibur_candidate() is None:\n513:             yield False\n514:         yield True\n515: \n516:         self.agent.go_to(*list(zip(*mask.nonzero()))[0])\n517: \n518:         candidate = excalibur_candidate()\n519:         if candidate is None:\n520:             return\n521: \n522:         # TODO: refactor\n523:         with self.agent.atom_operation():\n524:             candidate = self.agent.inventory.move_to_inventory(candidate)\n525:             self.agent.step(A.Command.DIP)\n526:             self.agent.type_text(self.agent.inventory.items.get_letter(candidate))\n527:             if ('What do you want to dip ' in self.agent.message and 'into?' in self.agent.message) or \\\n528:                     \"You don't have anything to dip \" in self.agent.message:\n529:                 raise AgentPanic('no fountain here')\n530: \n531:     def can_sacrify(self, item):\n532:         if not item.is_corpse() or item.comment == 'old':\n533:             return False\n534: \n535:         mname = MON.permonst(item.monster_id + nh.GLYPH_MON_OFF).mname\n536:         if (mname == 'pony' and self.agent.character.role in [Character.KNIGHT, Character.BARBARIAN]) or \\\n537:                 (mname == 'kitten' and self.agent.character.role == [Character.BARBARIAN, Character.WIZARD]) or \\\n538:                 (mname == 'little dog' and item.naming):  # little dogs are always named\n539:             # sufficient condition for being an initial pet\n540:             return False\n541: \n542:         # a chaotic character offering a corpse of its own race summons a demon lord (Juiblex,\n543:         # Orcus, ...) onto the altar; never offer same-race corpses, whatever the alignment.\n544:         # From github.com/eL1fe/nethacker@dc2765b.\n545:         mapping = {\n546:             Character.HUMAN: MON.M2_HUMAN | MON.M2_WERE,\n547:             Character.DWARF: MON.M2_DWARF,\n548:             Character.ELF: MON.M2_ELF,\n549:             Character.GNOME: MON.M2_GNOME,\n550:             Character.ORC: MON.M2_ORC,\n551:         }\n552:         f2 = MON.permonst(item.monster_id + nh.GLYPH_MON_OFF).mflags2\n553:         if (f2 & mapping[self.agent.character.race]) > 0:\n554:             return False\n555: \n556:         return True\n557: \n558:     @utils.debug_log('offer_corpses')\n559:     @Strategy.wrap\n560:     def offer_corpses(self):\n561:         self.item_priority._take_sacrificial_corpses = False\n562: \n563:         if self._got_artifact:\n564:             yield False\n565: \n566:         altars = [p for p, alignment in self.agent.current_level().altars.items()\n567:                   if alignment == self.agent.character.alignment]\n568: \n569:         if not altars:\n570:             yield False\n571: \n572:         dis = self.agent.bfs()\n573:         altars = [(y, x) for y, x in altars if dis[y, x] != -1]\n574: \n575:         if not altars:\n576:             yield False\n577: \n578:         self.item_priority._take_sacrificial_corpses = True\n579: \n580:         if not any((self.can_sacrify(item) for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items))):\n581:             yield False\n582: \n583:         yield True\n584: \n585:         y, x = min(altars, key=lambda p: dis[p])\n586:         self.agent.go_to(y, x)\n587:         with self.agent.panic_if_position_changes():\n588:             while 1:\n589:                 for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items):\n590:                     if self.can_sacrify(item):\n591:                         with self.agent.atom_operation():\n592:                             item = self.agent.inventory.move_to_inventory(item)\n593:                             assert self.can_sacrify(item)\n594:                             self.agent.step(A.Command.OFFER)\n595:                             while ('There is ' in self.agent.message or 'There are ' in self.agent.message) and \\\n596:                                     ('sacrifice it?' in self.agent.message or 'sacrifice one?' in self.agent.message):\n597:                                 self.agent.type_text('n')\n598:                             assert 'What do you want to sacrifice?' in self.agent.message, self.agent.message\n599:                             self.agent.type_text(self.agent.inventory.items.get_letter(item))\n600:                             if 'Nothing happens.' in self.agent.message:\n601:                                 self.agent.inventory.call_item(item, 'old')\n602:                                 return\n603:                             if 'Use my gift wisely' in self.agent.message:\n604:                                 self._got_artifact = True\n605:                                 self.agent.inventory.get_items_below_me()\n606:                                 return\n607:                             if 'So this is how you repay loyalty?' in self.agent.message:\n608:                                 raise AgentPanic('pet sacrified')\n609:                             assert 'Your sacrifice is consumed in a flash of light' in self.agent.message or \\\n610:                                 'Your sacrifice is consumed in a burst of flame' in self.agent.message or \\\n611:                                 ('The blood covers the altar!' in self.agent.message and \\\n612:                                  'You have summoned ' in self.agent.message), \\\n613:                                 self.agent.message\n614:                             break\n615:                 else:\n616:                     break\n617: \n618:     @utils.debug_log('follow_guard')\n619:     @Strategy.wrap\n620:     def follow_guard(self):\n621:         if not utils.isin(self.agent.glyphs, G.GUARD).any():\n622:             yield False\n623: \n624:         if any(item.category == nh.COIN_CLASS for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items)):\n625:             yield True\n626:             # if 'Please drop that gold and follow me.' in self.message:\n627:             self.agent.stats_logger.log_event('drop_gold')\n628:             self.item_priority._drop_gold_till_turn = self.agent.blstats.time + 100\n629:             self.agent.inventory.arrange_items().run()\n630:             return\n631: \n632:         ys, xs = utils.isin(self.agent.glyphs, G.GUARD).nonzero()\n633:         y, x = ys[0], xs[0]\n634: \n635:         if utils.adjacent((y, x), (self.agent.blstats.y, self.agent.blstats.x)):\n636:             yield False\n637: \n638:         yield True\n639: \n640:         self.agent.go_to(y, x, stop_one_before=True)\n641: \n642:     @Strategy.wrap\n643:     def current_strategy(self):\n644:         yield True\n645:         idle_iterations = 0\n646:         while 1:\n647:             explore_stairs_condition = lambda: False\n648:             if self.milestone == Milestone.BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL:\n649:                 # Dlvl 1 has few monsters and fewer corpses: a grind that runs out of food starves\n650:                 # there, fainting in front of the next pack of jackals. Hungry with nothing left to\n651:                 # eat, move on down where corpses (and experience) come faster.\n652:                 condition = lambda: self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= self._grind_xl() or \\\n653:                     (LEAVE_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY and\n654:                      self.agent.character.role in ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY and\n655:                      self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.HUNGRY and\n656:                      self.agent.inventory.items.total_nutrition() == 0)\n657:                 # explore_stairs_condition = lambda: self.agent.inventory.items.total_nutrition() == 0 and \\\n658:                 #                                    self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY\n659:                 level = (Level.DUNGEONS_OF_DOOM, 1)\n660: \n661:             elif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_SOKOBAN:\n662:                 condition = lambda: self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.SOKOBAN\n663:                 level = (Level.SOKOBAN, 4)\n664: \n665:             elif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_GNOMISH_MINES:\n666:                 condition = lambda: self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES\n667:                 level = (Level.GNOMISH_MINES, 1)\n668: \n669:             # elif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_LIGHT_GNOMISH_MINES:\n670:             #     condition = lambda: self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES \\\n671:             #             and self.agent.current_level().is_light_level()\n672:             #     level = (Level.GNOMISH_MINES, 9)\n673: \n674:             # elif self.milestone == Milestone.FARM_LIGHT_GNOMISH_MINES:\n675:             #     condition = lambda: self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= 11\n676:             #     level = (Level.GNOMISH_MINES, self.agent.current_level().level_number)\n677: \n678:             elif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN:\n679:                 condition = lambda: self.minetown_level is not None\n680:                 level = (Level.GNOMISH_MINES, 4)  # TODO\n681: \n682:             elif self.milestone == Milestone.SOLVE_SOKOBAN:\n683:                 # TODO: fix the condition, monster can destroy doors\n684:                 condition = lambda: self.agent.current_level().key() == (Level.SOKOBAN, 1) and \\\n685:                                     not utils.isin(self.agent.current_level().objects, G.DOOR_CLOSED).any()\n686:                 level = (Level.SOKOBAN, 1)\n687: \n688:             elif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINES_END:\n689:                 # the Mines are 8 or 9 levels deep, so waiting for level 9 left every 8-level Mines\n690:                 # stuck at its bottom forever; level 8 is the bottom or one short of it\n691:                 condition = lambda: self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES and \\\n692:                                     self.agent.current_level().level_number >= 8\n693:                 level = (Level.GNOMISH_MINES, 9)  # TODO\n694: \n695:             else:\n696:                 # TODO\n697:                 condition = lambda: False\n698:                 level = (Level.DUNGEONS_OF_DOOM, 100)\n699: \n700:             # a character that can dig heads straight down instead of grinding on Dlvl 1 (see\n701:             # Agent.dig_down); otherwise the Dlvl 1 milestone walks it back up after every hole\n702:             if self.milestone < Milestone.GO_DOWN and \\\n703:                     self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= early_dig_xl(self.agent.character) and \\\n704:                     self.agent.pick_for_digging() is not None:\n705:                 self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n706:                 continue\n707: \n708:             # a pick hunt in the upper Mines that has not paid off: dive by the stairs instead\n709:             if self.milestone in (Milestone.FIND_GNOMISH_MINES, Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN) and \\\n710:                     self._pick_hunt_start is not None and \\\n711:                     self.agent.blstats.time - self._pick_hunt_start > \\\n712:                     ROLE_PICK_HUNT_TURNS.get(self.agent.character.role, PICK_HUNT_TURNS):\n713:                 self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n714:                 continue\n715: \n716:             if condition():\n717:                 # hypothesis: after the Dlvl 1 grind to Xp 8 the deep phase heads into the Gnomish\n718:                 # Mines. For a gnome that is a safe road (most of the gnomes, dwarves and hill orcs\n719:                 # there are peaceful to it), but for any other race it is a gauntlet of hostile\n720:                 # packs on open cave levels that also bottom out at Mines' End (Dlvl 10-13), capping\n721:                 # the depth milestones -- the best-scoring part of the score. Non-gnomes instead\n722:                 # descend the main Dungeons of Doom (stairs, plus dig_down with any digging tool):\n723:                 # room-and-corridor levels where fights come one at a time and no floor until\n724:                 # Medusa. The switch happens only at the Xp 8 hand-off, so the grind is untouched.\n725:                 # Exception: races the Mines' dwarves are hostile to go there first, only as far\n726:                 # as Minetown, to kill dwarves for the pick-axe most of them carry -- with a pick\n727:                 # the milestone above switches to GO_DOWN and dig_down takes over in the main\n728:                 # dungeon. Dwarves and gnomes find those dwarves peaceful, so they skip the hunt and\n729:                 # instead walk the peaceful Mines straight to Mines' End (Dlvl 10-13), skipping the\n730:                 # long and risky Sokoban detour, before diving the main dungeon.\n731:                 race = self.agent.character.race\n732:                 mines_folk = MINES_FOLK_ROUTE and self._role_routes() and race in (Character.GNOME, Character.DWARF)\n733:                 if self.milestone == Milestone.BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL and race != Character.GNOME and \\\n734:                         not mines_folk:\n735:                     if PICK_HUNT_TURNS > 0 and self._role_routes() and race != Character.DWARF:\n736:                         self._pick_hunt_start = self.agent.blstats.time\n737:                         self.milestone = Milestone.FIND_GNOMISH_MINES\n738:                     else:\n739:                         self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n740:                     continue\n741:                 if self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN and self._pick_hunt_start is not None:\n742:                     self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n743:                     continue\n744:                 if self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN and mines_folk:\n745:                     self.milestone = Milestone.FIND_MINES_END\n746:                     continue\n747:                 self.milestone = Milestone(int(self.milestone) + 1)\n748:                 continue\n749: \n750: \n751:             def exploration_strategy(level, **kwargs):\n752:                 return (\n753:                     Strategy(lambda: self.agent.exploration.explore1(level, trap_search_offset=1,\n754:                         kick_doors=self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number != Level.GNOMISH_MINES, **kwargs).strategy())\n755:                     .preempt(self.agent, [\n756:                         self.identify_items_on_altar().every(100),\n757:                         self.identify_items_on_altar().condition(\n758:                             lambda: self.agent.current_level().objects[self.agent.blstats.y,\n759:                                                                        self.agent.blstats.x] in G.ALTAR),\n760:                         self.dip_for_excalibur().condition(\n761:                             lambda: self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= 7).every(10),\n762:                     ])\n763:                 )\n764: \n765:             def go_to_strategy(y, x):\n766:                 return (\n767:                     exploration_strategy(None)\n768:                     .preempt(self.agent, [\n769:                         self.agent.exploration.go_to_strategy(y, x).preempt(self.agent, [\n770:                             self.agent.inventory.gather_items(),\n771:                             self.identify_items_on_altar(),\n772:                             self.dip_for_excalibur().condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= 7),\n773:                         ])\n774:                         .condition(lambda: self._got_artifact or\n775:                                            not any([alignment == self.agent.character.alignment\n776:                                                     for _, alignment in self.agent.current_level().altars.items()]))\n777:                     ])\n778:                     .until(self.agent, lambda: (self.agent.blstats.y, self.agent.blstats.x) == (y, x))\n779:                 )\n780: \n781:             # The stock plan explores every level to exhaustion before moving on. On the huge dark\n782:             # Mines levels that never finishes: a Valkyrie that got its pick-axe on Mines level 1\n783:             # explored it for 9000 turns instead of walking up to the main dungeon to dig. When\n784:             # diving, skip the exhaustive pass and head for the level the plan wants.\n785:             def diving():\n786:                 return DIVE_SKIPS_EXPLORATION and self.milestone in (Milestone.GO_DOWN, Milestone.FIND_MINES_END) or \\\n787:                     (self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN and self._pick_hunt_start is None)\n788: \n789:             step_count_before = self.agent.step_count\n790:             (\n791:                 self.agent.exploration.go_to_level_strategy(*level, go_to_strategy, exploration_strategy(None))\n792:                 .before(exploration_strategy(None))#.before(self.agent.exploration.patrol())\n793:                 .preempt(self.agent, [\n794:                     exploration_strategy(0).condition(lambda: not diving()),\n795:                     exploration_strategy(None).until(\n796:                         self.agent, lambda: self.agent.blstats.hitpoints >= 0.8 * self.agent.blstats.max_hitpoints)\n797:                 ])\n798:                 .preempt(self.agent, [\n799:                     self.agent.exploration.explore_stairs(go_to_strategy, all=True).condition(explore_stairs_condition),\n800:                 ])\n801:                 .until(self.agent, condition)\n802:             ).run()\n803: \n804:             # hypothesis (see Agent.handle_exception): once the current level is fully explored and\n805:             # searched, every sub-strategy declines without acting while the milestone condition (e.g.\n806:             # Xp8 on Dlvl 1) is still unmet, so this loop spins forever without a single game action --\n807:             # the agent hangs, the game idles until the no-progress timeout and the run's remaining\n808:             # progress is forfeited. After many consecutive action-less passes, search in place so\n809:             # game time passes (monsters spawn and come to us, XP keeps growing) instead of hanging.\n810:             if self.agent.step_count == step_count_before:\n811:                 idle_iterations += 1\n812:                 if idle_iterations >= 20:\n813:                     idle_iterations = 0\n814:                     self.agent.search(10)\n815:             else:\n816:                 idle_iterations = 0\n817: \n818:     # hypothesis: gnomes and dwarves (cav/hea/ran-gno, val-dwa) walk the Mines after the Xp 8 grind\n819:     # among *peaceful* dwarves, so unlike every other race they never kill one for the pick-axe or\n820:     # mattock ~64% of them carry, and without a digging tool they dive by the stairs and die at\n821:     # Dlvl 2-10 (the Archeologist, who has a pick, averages Dlvl 17). Deliberately picking a fight\n822:     # with one peaceful dwarf is cheap: melee angers it before it dies, so there is no Luck\n823:     # penalty, only a few alignment points, and an Xp 8 character with most of its HP wins the\n824:     # fight. Once the pick is in the pack the existing machinery (milestone -> GO_DOWN, dig_down\n825:     # under Elbereth) turns the rest of the game into a dig dive. Only applies after the grind, so\n826:     # the Dlvl 1 game is byte-identical to the parent's.\n827:     # From github.com/Komershan/nethacker@d3d40a6.\n828:     @Strategy.wrap\n829:     def anger_peaceful_dwarf(self):\n830:         a = self.agent\n831:         if a.character.race not in (Character.GNOME, Character.DWARF) or \\\n832:                 self.milestone == Milestone.BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL or \\\n833:                 a.character.prop.hallu or a.character.prop.polymorph or \\\n834:                 a.blstats.hitpoints < 0.8 * a.blstats.max_hitpoints or \\\n835:                 a.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.WEAK or \\\n836:                 a.pick_for_digging() is not None:\n837:             yield False\n838:         level = a.current_level()\n839:         # never where the Watch or a shopkeeper could get involved\n840:         if (self.minetown_level is not None and level.key() == self.minetown_level) or \\\n841:                 utils.isin(a.glyphs, G.SHOPKEEPER).any() or level.shop[a.blstats.y, a.blstats.x]:\n842:             yield False\n843:         peaceful = a.monster_tracker.peaceful_monster_mask\n844:         dis = a.bfs()\n845:         best = None\n846:         for y, x in zip(*peaceful.nonzero()):\n847:             if not MON.is_monster(a.glyphs[y, x]):\n848:                 continue\n849:             name = MON.permonst(a.glyphs[y, x]).mname\n850:             if name.startswith('watch'):\n851:                 yield False\n852:             if name not in ('dwarf', 'dwarf lord', 'dwarf king'):\n853:                 continue\n854:             nd = dis[max(y - 1, 0):y + 2, max(x - 1, 0):x + 2]\n855:             nd = nd[nd != -1]\n856:             if nd.size == 0:\n857:                 continue\n858:             d = int(nd.min())\n859:             if d <= 12 and (best is None or d < best[0]):\n860:                 best = (d, y, x)\n861:         if best is None:\n862:             yield False\n863:         yield True\n864:         _, y, x = best\n865:         if utils.adjacent((y, x), (a.blstats.y, a.blstats.x)):\n866:             a.melee_attack(y, x)\n867:             # the tracker carries peacefulness over from the previous frame; force a fresh\n868:             # monster listing so fight2 sees the now hostile dwarf\n869:             a.monster_tracker.on_panic()\n870:             return\n871:         a.go_to(y, x, stop_one_before=True, max_steps=1)\n872: \n873:     def global_strategy(self):\n874:         return (\n875:             self.current_strategy().repeat()\n876:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n877:                 self.solve_sokoban_strategy()\n878:                 .condition(lambda: self.milestone == Milestone.SOLVE_SOKOBAN and\n879:                                    self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.SOKOBAN)\n880:             ])\n881:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n882:                 self.offer_corpses().preempt(self.agent, [\n883:                     self.agent.eat_corpses_from_ground().condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY),\n884:                 ]),\n885:             ])\n886:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n887:                 self.wait_out_unexpected_state_strategy(),\n888:             ])\n889:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n890:                 self.agent.cure_disease().every(5),\n891:             ])\n892:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n893:                 self.agent.eat_corpses_from_ground(only_below_me=True).condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY),\n894:                 self.agent.eat_corpses_from_ground().every(5).condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY),\n895:                 self.agent.eat_from_inventory().every(5),\n896:             ])\n897:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n898:                 self.follow_guard(),\n899:             ])\n900:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n901:                 self.anger_peaceful_dwarf(),\n902:             ])\n903:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n904:                 self.agent.fight2(),\n905:             ])\n906:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n907:                 self.agent.engulfed_fight(),\n908:             ])\n909:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n910:                 self.agent.proactive_sleep_strategy(),\n911:             ])\n912:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n913:                 self.agent.emergency_strategy(),\n914:             ])\n915:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n916:                 self.agent.read_magic_mapping(),\n917:             ])\n918:             .preempt(self.agent, [\n919:                 self.agent.dig_down(),\n920:             ])\n921:         )\n\n(End of file - total 921 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"from enum import IntEnum, auto\n\nimport nle.nethack as nh\nimport numpy as np\nfrom nle.nethack import actions as A\n\nfrom . import objects as O\nfrom . import soko_solver\nfrom . import utils\nfrom .character import Character\nfrom .exceptions import AgentPanic\nfrom .glyph import Hunger, G, MON\nfrom .item import Item, flatten_items\nfrom .item.item_priority_base import ItemPriorityBase\nfrom .level import Level\nfrom .strategy import Strategy\n\n\nclass ItemPriority(ItemPriorityBase):\n    MAX_NUMBER_OF_ITEMS = 26 * 2 - 1  # + coin slot, one slot should be left for item arranging","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/autoascend/global_logic.py","text":"from enum import IntEnum, auto\n\nimport nle.nethack as nh\nimport numpy as np\nfrom nle.nethack import actions as A\n\nfrom . import objects as O\nfrom . import soko_solver\nfrom . import utils\nfrom .character import Character\nfrom .exceptions import AgentPanic\nfrom .glyph import Hunger, G, MON\nfrom .item import Item, flatten_items\nfrom .item.item_priority_base import ItemPriorityBase\nfrom .level import Level\nfrom .strategy import Strategy\n\n\nclass ItemPriority(ItemPriorityBase):\n    MAX_NUMBER_OF_ITEMS = 26 * 2 - 1  # + coin slot, one slot should be left for item arranging\n    def __init__(self, agent):\n        self.agent = agent\n        self._take_sacrificial_corpses = False\n        self._drop_gold_till_turn = -float('inf')\n\n    def _split(self, items, forced_items, weight_capacity):\n        if self.agent.global_logic.squeeze_cap:\n            weight_capacity = min(weight_capacity, SQUEEZE_WEIGHT_CAP)\n        remaining_weight = weight_capacity\n        ret_inv = {}\n        for item in forced_items:\n            remaining_weight -= item.weight()\n            ret_inv[item] = item.count\n\n        ret_bag = {}\n        bag = None\n\n        def add_item(item, count=None, to_bag=False):\n            nonlocal ret_inv, ret_bag, remaining_weight\n            assert isinstance(item, Item)\n            if to_bag and bag is not None and item is not bag:\n                ret = ret_bag\n            else:\n                ret = ret_inv\n\n            if remaining_weight < 0 or \\\n                    (ret is ret_inv and len(ret) >= ItemPriority.MAX_NUMBER_OF_ITEMS):  # TODO: coin slot\n                return\n\n            how_many_already_total = ret_inv.get(item, 0) + ret_bag.get(item, 0)\n            how_many_already = ret.get(item, 0)\n            unit_weight = item.unit_weight(with_content=False)\n            # weightless items (e.g. wraith corpses) would make this an infinite count\n            max_to_add = item.count if unit_weight <= 0 else int(remaining_weight // unit_weight)\n            if count is not None:\n                max_to_add = min(max_to_add, count)\n            ret[item] = min(item.count, how_many_already_total + max_to_add) - (how_many_already_total - how_many_already)\n            remaining_weight -= item.unit_weight(with_content=False) * (ret[item] - how_many_already)\n\n        for item in items:\n            if item.is_container() and item.status in [Item.UNCURSED, Item.BLESSED] and item.objs[0].desc == 'bag':\n                bag = item  # TODO: select the best\n                add_item(bag)\n\n        if self._drop_gold_till_turn < self.agent.blstats.time:\n            for item in items:\n                if item.category == nh.COIN_CLASS:\n                    add_item(item)\n\n        def add_pick():\n            for item in items:\n                if item.is_unambiguous() and item.objs[0].name in ('pick-axe', 'dwarvish mattock') and \\\n                        item.status != Item.CURSED:\n                    add_item(item)\n                    break\n\n        # squeezing through is only needed to get the pick back to the main dungeon, so under the\n        # squeeze cap it goes first\n        if self.agent.global_logic.squeeze_cap:\n            add_pick()\n\n        for allow_unknown_status in [False, True]:\n            item = self.agent.inventory.get_best_melee_weapon(items=forced_items + items,\n                                                              allow_unknown_status=allow_unknown_status)\n            if item is not None:\n                add_item(item)\n\n            for item in self.agent.inventory.get_best_armorset(items=forced_items + items,\n                                                               allow_unknown_status=allow_unknown_status):\n                if item is not None:\n                    add_item(item)\n\n        # a digging tool turns the rest of the game into a dive (Agent.dig_down), worth far more than\n        # anything else we could carry in its weight\n        add_pick()\n\n        for item in items:\n            if item.is_unambiguous():\n                if item.object in [\n                        O.from_name('healing', nh.POTION_CLASS),\n                        O.from_name('extra healing', nh.POTION_CLASS),\n                        O.from_name('full healing', nh.POTION_CLASS)]:\n                    add_item(item)\n\n                if self.agent.character.role in [Character.RANGER, Character.ROGUE,\n                                                 Character.SAMURAI, Character.TOURIST] and \\\n                        (item.is_launcher() or item.is_fired_projectile()):\n                    add_item(item)\n\n        if self.agent.character.alignment == Character.LAWFUL:\n            for item in sorted(filter(lambda i: i.objs[0].name == 'long sword', items),\n                               key=lambda i: -utils.calc_dps(*self.agent.character.get_melee_bonus(i))):\n                add_item(item)\n                break\n\n        for item in sorted(filter(lambda i: i.is_thrown_projectile(), items),\n                           key=lambda i: -utils.calc_dps(*self.agent.character.get_ranged_bonus(None, i))):\n            add_item(item)\n\n        for item in sorted(filter(lambda i: i.is_food() and not i.is_corpse(), items),\n                           key=lambda x: -x.nutrition_per_weight() - 1000 * (x.objs[0].name == 'sprig of wolfsbane')):\n            add_item(item)\n\n        if self._take_sacrificial_corpses:\n            for item in filter(self.agent.global_logic.can_sacrify, items):\n                add_item(item)\n\n        # TODO: take nh.COIN_CLASS once shopping is implemented.\n        # You have to drop all coins not to be attacked by a vault guard\n\n        for item in sorted(items, key=lambda i: i.unit_weight(with_content=False)):\n            if item.category in [nh.POTION_CLASS, nh.RING_CLASS, nh.AMULET_CLASS, nh.WAND_CLASS, nh.SCROLL_CLASS, nh.TOOL_CLASS]:\n                if (not isinstance(item.objs[0], O.Container) or not item.is_chest()) and \\\n                        not item.is_possible_container():\n                    to_bag = O.from_name('cancellation', nh.WAND_CLASS) not in item.objs and \\\n                             not item.is_offensive_usable_wand()\n                    to_bag = False\n                    if not item.is_container():  # remove condition to pick up bags\n                        add_item(item, to_bag=to_bag)\n\n        categories = [nh.WEAPON_CLASS, nh.ARMOR_CLASS, nh.TOOL_CLASS, nh.FOOD_CLASS, nh.GEM_CLASS, nh.AMULET_CLASS,\n                      nh.RING_CLASS, nh.POTION_CLASS, nh.SCROLL_CLASS, nh.SPBOOK_CLASS, nh.WAND_CLASS]\n        for item in sorted(items, key=lambda i: i.unit_weight(with_content=False)):\n            if item.category in categories and not isinstance(item.objs[0], O.Container) and not item.is_corpse():\n                if item.status == Item.UNKNOWN:\n                    to_bag = O.from_name('cancellation', nh.WAND_CLASS) not in item.objs and \\\n                             not item.is_offensive_usable_wand()\n                    to_bag = False\n                    if not item.is_container():  # remove condition to pick up bags\n                        add_item(item, to_bag=to_bag)\n\n        r = {None: [ret_inv.get(item, 0) for item in items]}\n        if bag is not None:\n            r[bag] = [ret_bag.get(item, 0) for item in items]\n        for item in items:\n            if item.is_container() and item is not bag and ret_inv.get(item, 0) != 0:\n                r[item] = [0 for _ in items]\n        return r\n\n\nclass Milestone(IntEnum):\n    BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL = auto()\n    FIND_GNOMISH_MINES = auto()\n    # FIND_LIGHT_GNOMISH_MINES = auto()\n    # FARM_LIGHT_GNOMISH_MINES = auto()\n    FIND_MINETOWN = auto()\n    FIND_SOKOBAN = auto()\n    SOLVE_SOKOBAN = auto()\n    FIND_MINES_END = auto()\n    GO_DOWN = auto() # TODO\n\n\n# experience level from which a character carrying a pick-axe skips the Dlvl 1 grind and digs down\nEARLY_DIG_XL = 3\n# turns a non-gnome, non-dwarf spends hunting the Mines' dwarves for a pick-axe after the Dlvl 1\n# grind before it gives up and dives by the stairs; 0 disables the hunt\nPICK_HUNT_TURNS = 3000\n# roles whose pick hunt paid off when doubled (73-identity A/B)\nROLE_PICK_HUNT_TURNS = {}\n# NetHack refuses a diagonal squeeze between two rock squares to anyone carrying more than 600\nSQUEEZE_WEIGHT_LIMIT = 600\n# the inventory budget once squeezing is needed, a little under the limit for weight misestimates\nSQUEEZE_WEIGHT_CAP = 580\n# experience level the Dlvl 1 grind stops at before the deep phase begins\nGRIND_XL = 8\n# gnomes and dwarves walk the peaceful Mines to Mines' End before diving the main dungeon\nMINES_FOLK_ROUTE = True\n# Per-role overrides picked from a 73-identity A/B on the public seeds (Xp 5 vs Xp 8 grind,\n# with and without the Mines routes): fighters and fragile casters both do better grinding\n# to Xp 8 first; Rogues and Samurai dive the main dungeon without the Mines detours.\n# A later sweep over Xp 5/6/7/8 moved Knights and Valkyries to 7 and Healers to 6.\nROLE_GRIND_XL = {}\n# Xp from which a character carrying a pick digs down, where it differs from EARLY_DIG_XL\n# (a Monk-only Xp 8 dig, as in github.com/eL1fe/nethacker@ff8e491, measured worse here)\nROLE_EARLY_DIG_XL = {}\n# ablation switches for fixes made while diving (see their call sites)\nDIVE_SKIPS_EXPLORATION = True\nLEAVE_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY = False\n# Roles for which leaving the Dlvl 1 grind when out of food pays (73-identity A/B): the others\n# (Healers, Knights, Priests, Rogues, Tourists, Valkyries) do better finishing the grind.\nROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY = {Character.ARCHEOLOGIST, Character.BARBARIAN, Character.CAVEMAN,\n                                   Character.RANGER, Character.SAMURAI, Character.MONK,\n                                   Character.WIZARD}\n\n\ndef early_dig_xl(character):\n    return ROLE_EARLY_DIG_XL.get(character.role, EARLY_DIG_XL)\n\nROLES_WITHOUT_MINES_ROUTES = {Character.ROGUE, Character.SAMURAI}\n\n\nclass GlobalLogic:\n    def __init__(self, agent):\n        self.agent = agent\n        self.milestone = Milestone(1)\n        self._pick_hunt_start = None  # turn the Mines pick hunt began, if it did\n        self.step_completion_log = {}  # Milestone -> (step, turn)\n\n        self.item_priority = ItemPriority(self.agent)\n\n        self.oracle_level = None\n        self.minetown_level = None\n\n        self._got_artifact = False\n\n        self.squeeze_cap = False  # carry at most SQUEEZE_WEIGHT_CAP (see _update_squeeze_cap)\n        self._squeeze_hits = 0\n        self._squeeze_check_turn = -float('inf')\n\n    def _grind_xl(self):\n        return ROLE_GRIND_XL.get(self.agent.character.role, GRIND_XL)\n\n    def _role_routes(self):\n        return self.agent.character.role not in ROLES_WITHOUT_MINES_ROUTES\n\n    def _update_squeeze_cap(self):\n        # hypothesis: a pick hunter that wins its digging tool in the Gnomish Mines often never turns\n        # it into a dive, stalling on a Mines level for 5k-20k turns and scoring only its Xp\n        # (~0.05-0.18) instead of the Dlvl 10-26 dive (0.13-0.5). Three things hold it there:\n        # 1. the bot fills its pack to its carrying capacity (usually 700-1000, and the pick adds\n        #    100-120), but NetHack forbids squeezing diagonally between two rock squares to anyone\n        #    carrying over 600, and the Mines' cave levels are full of such gaps, so the up stairs\n        #    are often unreachable. When a staircase of a Mines level stays reachable only by\n        #    squeezing, cap the pack below the limit (the pick first) for the rest of the Mines\n        #    visit, so the bot drops its least valued items and walks on (this method);\n        # 2. before heading for the stairs it first explores every corner of each item-strewn Mines\n        #    level, which with the fights and pickups along the way takes thousands of turns\n        #    (_leaving_mines_to_dig);\n        # 3. a dwarvish mattock is two-handed and cannot be applied under a shield, so a hunter\n        #    whose tool is a mattock tries to dig and fails on every square\n        #    (Inventory.get_best_armorset, Agent.pick_for_digging).\n        # Outside the Mines and without a digging tool nothing changes.\n        level = self.agent.current_level()\n        if level.dungeon_number != Level.GNOMISH_MINES:\n            self.squeeze_cap = False\n            self._squeeze_hits = 0\n            return\n        if self.squeeze_cap or self.agent.inventory.items.total_weight <= SQUEEZE_WEIGHT_LIMIT:\n            return\n        turn = self.agent.blstats.time\n        if turn - self._squeeze_check_turn < 10:\n            return\n        self._squeeze_check_turn = turn\n        only_squeezing = (self.agent.bfs(can_squeeze=True) != -1) & (self.agent.bfs(can_squeeze=False) == -1)\n        # a monster standing in a gap looks the same, and exploring may still turn up another way\n        # around, so the cut-off has to persist for a while\n        if (only_squeezing & utils.isin(level.objects, G.STAIR_UP, G.STAIR_DOWN)).any():\n            self._squeeze_hits += 1\n        else:\n            self._squeeze_hits = 0\n        if self._squeeze_hits >= 50:\n            self.squeeze_cap = True\n\n    def _leaving_mines_to_dig(self):\n        # (see _update_squeeze_cap) with the digging tool in hand the Mines level has nothing left\n        # to offer: walk straight back to the main dungeon rather than first exploring every corner\n        # of this item-strewn cave level, which with fights and pickups can take thousands of turns\n        return self.milestone == Milestone.GO_DOWN and \\\n               self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES and \\\n               self.agent.pick_for_digging() is not None\n\n    def update(self):\n        self._update_squeeze_cap()\n        if not self.agent.character.prop.hallu:\n            if utils.isin(self.agent.glyphs, G.ORACLE).any():\n                if self.oracle_level is None:\n                    self.oracle_level = self.agent.current_level().key()\n                else:\n                    assert self.oracle_level == self.agent.current_level().key()\n\n            if self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES and \\\n                    utils.isin(self.agent.glyphs, G.SHOPKEEPER).any():\n                if self.minetown_level is None:\n                    self.minetown_level = self.agent.current_level().key()\n                else:\n                    assert self.minetown_level == self.agent.current_level().key()\n\n    @utils.debug_log('solving sokoban')\n    @Strategy.wrap\n    def solve_sokoban_strategy(self):\n        # TODO: refactor\n        if not utils.isin(self.agent.current_level().objects, G.TRAPS).any():\n            yield False\n        yield True\n\n        def push_bolder(ty, tx, dy, dx):\n            while 1:\n                if self.agent.bfs()[ty, tx] == -1:\n                    return False\n                self.agent.go_to(ty, tx, debug_tiles_args=dict(color=(255, 255, 255), is_path=True))\n                with self.agent.atom_operation():\n                    direction = self.agent.calc_direction(ty, tx, ty + dy, tx + dx)\n                    self.agent.direction(direction)\n                    message = self.agent.message\n\n                if (self.agent.blstats.y, self.agent.blstats.x) == (ty, tx):\n                    assert 'You hear a monster behind the boulder.' in message or \\\n                           'You try to move the boulder, but in vain.' in message, message\n                    if self.agent.bfs()[ty + dy, tx + dx] != -1:\n                        self.agent.go_to(ty + dy, tx + dx, debug_tiles_args=dict(color=(255, 255, 255), is_path=True))\n                        continue\n                    else:\n                        pickaxe = None\n                        for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items):\n                            if item.is_unambiguous() and \\\n                                    item.object in [O.from_name('pick-axe'), O.from_name('dwarvish mattock')]:\n                                pickaxe = item\n                                break\n                        if pickaxe is not None:\n                            with self.agent.atom_operation():\n                                pickaxe = self.agent.inventory.move_to_inventory(pickaxe)\n                                self.agent.step(A.Command.APPLY)\n                                self.agent.type_text(self.agent.inventory.items.get_letter(pickaxe))\n                                self.agent.direction(direction)\n                            return True\n                else:\n                    return True\n\n                # TODO: not sure what to do\n                self.agent.exploration.explore1(None).run()\n\n        while 1:\n            wall_map = utils.isin(self.agent.current_level().objects, G.WALL)\n            for smap, answer in soko_solver.maps.items():\n                sokomap = soko_solver.convert_map(smap)\n                offset = np.array(min(zip(*wall_map.nonzero()))) - \\\n                         np.array(min(zip(*(sokomap.sokomap == soko_solver.WALL).nonzero())))\n                mask = wall_map[offset[0] : offset[0] + sokomap.sokomap.shape[0],\n                                offset[1] : offset[1] + sokomap.sokomap.shape[1]]\n                if (mask & (sokomap.sokomap == soko_solver.WALL) == mask).all():\n                    break\n            else:\n                assert 0, 'sokomap not found'\n\n            def simulate_move(y, x, dy, dx):\n                # the real level diverged from the solver (a boulder got destroyed,\n                # displaced or buried), so the stored solution no longer applies\n                try:\n                    sokomap.move(y, x, dy, dx)\n                except AssertionError:\n                    self.agent.stats_logger.log_event('sokoban_dropped')\n                    self.milestone = Milestone(int(self.milestone) + 1)\n                    raise AgentPanic('sokomap desynced')\n\n            possible_mimics = set()\n            last_resort_move = None\n            for (y, x), (dy, dx) in answer:\n                boulder_map = utils.isin(self.agent.glyphs, G.BOULDER)\n                mask = boulder_map[offset[0] : offset[0] + sokomap.sokomap.shape[0],\n                                   offset[1] : offset[1] + sokomap.sokomap.shape[1]]\n                ty, tx = offset[0] + y - dy, offset[1] + x - dx,\n                soko_boulder_mask = sokomap.sokomap == soko_solver.BOULDER\n                if self.agent.bfs()[ty, tx] != -1 and \\\n                        ((soko_boulder_mask | mask) == soko_boulder_mask).all() and \\\n                        self.agent.glyphs[ty + dy, tx + dx] in G.BOULDER:\n\n                    soko_dis1 = sokomap.bfs()\n                    simulate_move(y, x, dy, dx)\n                    soko_dis2 = sokomap.bfs()\n\n                    # see points that will no longer be accessible\n                    with self.agent.env.debug_log('checking for monsters'):\n                        to_visit_mask = self.agent.bfs() != -1\n                        to_visit_mask[offset[0] : offset[0] + sokomap.sokomap.shape[0],\n                                      offset[1] : offset[1] + sokomap.sokomap.shape[1]] &= \\\n                                              (soko_dis1 != -1) & (soko_dis2 == -1)\n\n                        with self.agent.env.debug_tiles(to_visit_mask, color=(255, 0, 0, 128)):\n                            while to_visit_mask.any():\n                                vy, vx = list(zip(*to_visit_mask.nonzero()))[0]\n                                to_visit_mask[vy, vx] = 0\n\n                                def clear_neighbors():\n                                    to_visit_mask[self.agent.blstats.y, self.agent.blstats.x] = 0\n                                    to_visit_mask[utils.isin(self.agent.glyphs, G.VISIBLE_FLOOR)] = 0\n                                    return not to_visit_mask[vy, vx]\n\n                                self.agent.go_to(vy, vx, callback=clear_neighbors)\n\n                    if not push_bolder(ty, tx, dy, dx):\n                        continue\n\n                    possible_mimics = set()\n                    last_resort_move = None\n\n                    if not utils.isin(self.agent.current_level().objects, G.TRAPS).any():\n                        return\n\n                else:\n                    simulate_move(y, x, dy, dx)\n\n                if (~soko_boulder_mask | mask).all():\n                    if self.agent.bfs()[ty, tx] != -1 and \\\n                            self.agent.glyphs[ty + dy, tx + dx] in G.BOULDER and \\\n                            last_resort_move is None:\n                        last_resort_move = (ty, tx, dy, dx)\n\n                    if not possible_mimics:\n                        for mim_y, mim_x in zip(*(~soko_boulder_mask & mask).nonzero()):\n                            possible_mimics.add((mim_y + offset[0], mim_x + offset[1]))\n\n\n            # sokoban configuration is not in the list. Check for mimics\n            with self.agent.env.debug_log('mimics'):\n                with self.agent.env.debug_tiles(possible_mimics, color=(255, 0, 0, 128)):\n                    for mim_y, mim_x in sorted(possible_mimics):\n                        if (self.agent.bfs()[max(0, mim_y - 1) : mim_y + 2, max(0, mim_x - 1) : mim_x + 2] != -1).any():\n                            self.agent.go_to(mim_y, mim_x, stop_one_before=True,\n                                             debug_tiles_args=dict(color=(255, 0, 0), is_path=True))\n                            for _ in range(3):\n                                self.agent.search()\n\n            # last resort move (sometimes we can see a mimic diagonally but cannot reach it)\n            with self.agent.env.debug_log('last_resort'):\n                if last_resort_move is not None:\n                    ty, tx, dy, dx = last_resort_move\n                    push_bolder(ty, tx, dy, dx)\n                    continue\n\n            self.agent.stats_logger.log_event('sokoban_dropped')\n            self.milestone = Milestone(int(self.milestone) + 1)\n            raise AgentPanic('sokomap unsolvable')\n\n    @Strategy.wrap\n    def wait_out_unexpected_state_strategy(self):\n        yielded = False\n        while (\n                self.agent.character.prop.blind or\n                self.agent.character.prop.confusion or\n                self.agent.character.prop.stun or\n                self.agent.character.prop.hallu or\n                self.agent.character.prop.polymorph):\n            if not yielded:\n                yield True\n                yielded = True\n\n            self.agent.direction('.')\n\n        if not yielded:\n            yield False\n\n    @utils.debug_log('identify_items_on_altar')\n    @Strategy.wrap\n    def identify_items_on_altar(self):\n        mask = utils.isin(self.agent.current_level().objects, G.ALTAR)\n        if not mask.any():\n            yield False\n\n        dis = self.agent.bfs()\n        mask &= dis != -1\n        if not mask.any():\n            yield False\n\n        yield any((item.status == Item.UNKNOWN for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items)\n                   if item.can_be_dropped_from_inventory()))\n\n        (ty, tx), *_ = zip(*(mask & (dis == dis[mask].min())).nonzero())\n        self.agent.go_to(ty, tx)\n        items_to_drop = [item for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items)\n                         if item.can_be_dropped_from_inventory() and item.status == Item.UNKNOWN]\n        if not items_to_drop:\n            raise AgentPanic('items to drop on altar vanished')\n\n        # TODO: move chunking to inventory.drop\n        items_to_drop = items_to_drop[:self.agent.inventory.items.free_slots()]\n\n        self.agent.inventory.drop(items_to_drop)\n\n    @utils.debug_log('dip_for_excalibur')\n    @Strategy.wrap\n    def dip_for_excalibur(self):\n        if self.agent.character.alignment != Character.LAWFUL or self.agent.blstats.experience_level < 5:\n            yield False\n        if self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES and \\\n                (self.minetown_level is None or self.agent.current_level().key() == self.minetown_level):\n            yield False\n\n        dis = self.agent.bfs()\n        mask = utils.isin(self.agent.current_level().objects, G.FOUNTAIN) & (dis != -1)\n        if not mask.any():\n            yield False\n\n        def excalibur_candidate():\n            candidate = None\n            for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items):\n                if item.is_unambiguous() and item.object == O.from_name('long sword'):\n                    if item.dmg_bonus is not None: # TODO: better condition for excalibur existance\n                        return None\n                    candidate = item\n            return candidate\n\n        if excalibur_candidate() is None:\n            yield False\n        yield True\n\n        self.agent.go_to(*list(zip(*mask.nonzero()))[0])\n\n        candidate = excalibur_candidate()\n        if candidate is None:\n            return\n\n        # TODO: refactor\n        with self.agent.atom_operation():\n            candidate = self.agent.inventory.move_to_inventory(candidate)\n            self.agent.step(A.Command.DIP)\n            self.agent.type_text(self.agent.inventory.items.get_letter(candidate))\n            if ('What do you want to dip ' in self.agent.message and 'into?' in self.agent.message) or \\\n                    \"You don't have anything to dip \" in self.agent.message:\n                raise AgentPanic('no fountain here')\n\n    def can_sacrify(self, item):\n        if not item.is_corpse() or item.comment == 'old':\n            return False\n\n        mname = MON.permonst(item.monster_id + nh.GLYPH_MON_OFF).mname\n        if (mname == 'pony' and self.agent.character.role in [Character.KNIGHT, Character.BARBARIAN]) or \\\n                (mname == 'kitten' and self.agent.character.role == [Character.BARBARIAN, Character.WIZARD]) or \\\n                (mname == 'little dog' and item.naming):  # little dogs are always named\n            # sufficient condition for being an initial pet\n            return False\n\n        # a chaotic character offering a corpse of its own race summons a demon lord (Juiblex,\n        # Orcus, ...) onto the altar; never offer same-race corpses, whatever the alignment.\n        # From github.com/eL1fe/nethacker@dc2765b.\n        mapping = {\n            Character.HUMAN: MON.M2_HUMAN | MON.M2_WERE,\n            Character.DWARF: MON.M2_DWARF,\n            Character.ELF: MON.M2_ELF,\n            Character.GNOME: MON.M2_GNOME,\n            Character.ORC: MON.M2_ORC,\n        }\n        f2 = MON.permonst(item.monster_id + nh.GLYPH_MON_OFF).mflags2\n        if (f2 & mapping[self.agent.character.race]) > 0:\n            return False\n\n        return True\n\n    @utils.debug_log('offer_corpses')\n    @Strategy.wrap\n    def offer_corpses(self):\n        self.item_priority._take_sacrificial_corpses = False\n\n        if self._got_artifact:\n            yield False\n\n        altars = [p for p, alignment in self.agent.current_level().altars.items()\n                  if alignment == self.agent.character.alignment]\n\n        if not altars:\n            yield False\n\n        dis = self.agent.bfs()\n        altars = [(y, x) for y, x in altars if dis[y, x] != -1]\n\n        if not altars:\n            yield False\n\n        self.item_priority._take_sacrificial_corpses = True\n\n        if not any((self.can_sacrify(item) for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items))):\n            yield False\n\n        yield True\n\n        y, x = min(altars, key=lambda p: dis[p])\n        self.agent.go_to(y, x)\n        with self.agent.panic_if_position_changes():\n            while 1:\n                for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items):\n                    if self.can_sacrify(item):\n                        with self.agent.atom_operation():\n                            item = self.agent.inventory.move_to_inventory(item)\n                            assert self.can_sacrify(item)\n                            self.agent.step(A.Command.OFFER)\n                            while ('There is ' in self.agent.message or 'There are ' in self.agent.message) and \\\n                                    ('sacrifice it?' in self.agent.message or 'sacrifice one?' in self.agent.message):\n                                self.agent.type_text('n')\n                            assert 'What do you want to sacrifice?' in self.agent.message, self.agent.message\n                            self.agent.type_text(self.agent.inventory.items.get_letter(item))\n                            if 'Nothing happens.' in self.agent.message:\n                                self.agent.inventory.call_item(item, 'old')\n                                return\n                            if 'Use my gift wisely' in self.agent.message:\n                                self._got_artifact = True\n                                self.agent.inventory.get_items_below_me()\n                                return\n                            if 'So this is how you repay loyalty?' in self.agent.message:\n                                raise AgentPanic('pet sacrified')\n                            assert 'Your sacrifice is consumed in a flash of light' in self.agent.message or \\\n                                'Your sacrifice is consumed in a burst of flame' in self.agent.message or \\\n                                ('The blood covers the altar!' in self.agent.message and \\\n                                 'You have summoned ' in self.agent.message), \\\n                                self.agent.message\n                            break\n                else:\n                    break\n\n    @utils.debug_log('follow_guard')\n    @Strategy.wrap\n    def follow_guard(self):\n        if not utils.isin(self.agent.glyphs, G.GUARD).any():\n            yield False\n\n        if any(item.category == nh.COIN_CLASS for item in flatten_items(self.agent.inventory.items)):\n            yield True\n            # if 'Please drop that gold and follow me.' in self.message:\n            self.agent.stats_logger.log_event('drop_gold')\n            self.item_priority._drop_gold_till_turn = self.agent.blstats.time + 100\n            self.agent.inventory.arrange_items().run()\n            return\n\n        ys, xs = utils.isin(self.agent.glyphs, G.GUARD).nonzero()\n        y, x = ys[0], xs[0]\n\n        if utils.adjacent((y, x), (self.agent.blstats.y, self.agent.blstats.x)):\n            yield False\n\n        yield True\n\n        self.agent.go_to(y, x, stop_one_before=True)\n\n    @Strategy.wrap\n    def current_strategy(self):\n        yield True\n        idle_iterations = 0\n        while 1:\n            explore_stairs_condition = lambda: False\n            if self.milestone == Milestone.BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL:\n                # Dlvl 1 has few monsters and fewer corpses: a grind that runs out of food starves\n                # there, fainting in front of the next pack of jackals. Hungry with nothing left to\n                # eat, move on down where corpses (and experience) come faster.\n                condition = lambda: self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= self._grind_xl() or \\\n                    (LEAVE_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY and\n                     self.agent.character.role in ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY and\n                     self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.HUNGRY and\n                     self.agent.inventory.items.total_nutrition() == 0)\n                # explore_stairs_condition = lambda: self.agent.inventory.items.total_nutrition() == 0 and \\\n                #                                    self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY\n                level = (Level.DUNGEONS_OF_DOOM, 1)\n\n            elif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_SOKOBAN:\n                condition = lambda: self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.SOKOBAN\n                level = (Level.SOKOBAN, 4)\n\n            elif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_GNOMISH_MINES:\n                condition = lambda: self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES\n                level = (Level.GNOMISH_MINES, 1)\n\n            # elif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_LIGHT_GNOMISH_MINES:\n            #     condition = lambda: self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES \\\n            #             and self.agent.current_level().is_light_level()\n            #     level = (Level.GNOMISH_MINES, 9)\n\n            # elif self.milestone == Milestone.FARM_LIGHT_GNOMISH_MINES:\n            #     condition = lambda: self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= 11\n            #     level = (Level.GNOMISH_MINES, self.agent.current_level().level_number)\n\n            elif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN:\n                condition = lambda: self.minetown_level is not None\n                level = (Level.GNOMISH_MINES, 4)  # TODO\n\n            elif self.milestone == Milestone.SOLVE_SOKOBAN:\n                # TODO: fix the condition, monster can destroy doors\n                condition = lambda: self.agent.current_level().key() == (Level.SOKOBAN, 1) and \\\n                                    not utils.isin(self.agent.current_level().objects, G.DOOR_CLOSED).any()\n                level = (Level.SOKOBAN, 1)\n\n            elif self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINES_END:\n                # the Mines are 8 or 9 levels deep, so waiting for level 9 left every 8-level Mines\n                # stuck at its bottom forever; level 8 is the bottom or one short of it\n                condition = lambda: self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.GNOMISH_MINES and \\\n                                    self.agent.current_level().level_number >= 8\n                level = (Level.GNOMISH_MINES, 9)  # TODO\n\n            else:\n                # TODO\n                condition = lambda: False\n                level = (Level.DUNGEONS_OF_DOOM, 100)\n\n            # a character that can dig heads straight down instead of grinding on Dlvl 1 (see\n            # Agent.dig_down); otherwise the Dlvl 1 milestone walks it back up after every hole\n            if self.milestone < Milestone.GO_DOWN and \\\n                    self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= early_dig_xl(self.agent.character) and \\\n                    self.agent.pick_for_digging() is not None:\n                self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n                continue\n\n            # a pick hunt in the upper Mines that has not paid off: dive by the stairs instead\n            if self.milestone in (Milestone.FIND_GNOMISH_MINES, Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN) and \\\n                    self._pick_hunt_start is not None and \\\n                    self.agent.blstats.time - self._pick_hunt_start > \\\n                    ROLE_PICK_HUNT_TURNS.get(self.agent.character.role, PICK_HUNT_TURNS):\n                self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n                continue\n\n            if condition():\n                # hypothesis: after the Dlvl 1 grind to Xp 8 the deep phase heads into the Gnomish\n                # Mines. For a gnome that is a safe road (most of the gnomes, dwarves and hill orcs\n                # there are peaceful to it), but for any other race it is a gauntlet of hostile\n                # packs on open cave levels that also bottom out at Mines' End (Dlvl 10-13), capping\n                # the depth milestones -- the best-scoring part of the score. Non-gnomes instead\n                # descend the main Dungeons of Doom (stairs, plus dig_down with any digging tool):\n                # room-and-corridor levels where fights come one at a time and no floor until\n                # Medusa. The switch happens only at the Xp 8 hand-off, so the grind is untouched.\n                # Exception: races the Mines' dwarves are hostile to go there first, only as far\n                # as Minetown, to kill dwarves for the pick-axe most of them carry -- with a pick\n                # the milestone above switches to GO_DOWN and dig_down takes over in the main\n                # dungeon. Dwarves and gnomes find those dwarves peaceful, so they skip the hunt and\n                # instead walk the peaceful Mines straight to Mines' End (Dlvl 10-13), skipping the\n                # long and risky Sokoban detour, before diving the main dungeon.\n                race = self.agent.character.race\n                mines_folk = MINES_FOLK_ROUTE and self._role_routes() and race in (Character.GNOME, Character.DWARF)\n                if self.milestone == Milestone.BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL and race != Character.GNOME and \\\n                        not mines_folk:\n                    if PICK_HUNT_TURNS > 0 and self._role_routes() and race != Character.DWARF:\n                        self._pick_hunt_start = self.agent.blstats.time\n                        self.milestone = Milestone.FIND_GNOMISH_MINES\n                    else:\n                        self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n                    continue\n                if self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN and self._pick_hunt_start is not None:\n                    self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n                    continue\n                if self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN and mines_folk:\n                    self.milestone = Milestone.FIND_MINES_END\n                    continue\n                self.milestone = Milestone(int(self.milestone) + 1)\n                continue\n\n\n            def exploration_strategy(level, **kwargs):\n                return (\n                    Strategy(lambda: self.agent.exploration.explore1(level, trap_search_offset=1,\n                        kick_doors=self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number != Level.GNOMISH_MINES, **kwargs).strategy())\n                    .preempt(self.agent, [\n                        self.identify_items_on_altar().every(100),\n                        self.identify_items_on_altar().condition(\n                            lambda: self.agent.current_level().objects[self.agent.blstats.y,\n                                                                       self.agent.blstats.x] in G.ALTAR),\n                        self.dip_for_excalibur().condition(\n                            lambda: self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= 7).every(10),\n                    ])\n                )\n\n            def go_to_strategy(y, x):\n                return (\n                    exploration_strategy(None)\n                    .preempt(self.agent, [\n                        self.agent.exploration.go_to_strategy(y, x).preempt(self.agent, [\n                            self.agent.inventory.gather_items(),\n                            self.identify_items_on_altar(),\n                            self.dip_for_excalibur().condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.experience_level >= 7),\n                        ])\n                        .condition(lambda: self._got_artifact or\n                                           not any([alignment == self.agent.character.alignment\n                                                    for _, alignment in self.agent.current_level().altars.items()]))\n                    ])\n                    .until(self.agent, lambda: (self.agent.blstats.y, self.agent.blstats.x) == (y, x))\n                )\n\n            # The stock plan explores every level to exhaustion before moving on. On the huge dark\n            # Mines levels that never finishes: a Valkyrie that got its pick-axe on Mines level 1\n            # explored it for 9000 turns instead of walking up to the main dungeon to dig. When\n            # diving, skip the exhaustive pass and head for the level the plan wants.\n            def diving():\n                return DIVE_SKIPS_EXPLORATION and self.milestone in (Milestone.GO_DOWN, Milestone.FIND_MINES_END) or \\\n                    (self.milestone == Milestone.FIND_MINETOWN and self._pick_hunt_start is None)\n\n            step_count_before = self.agent.step_count\n            (\n                self.agent.exploration.go_to_level_strategy(*level, go_to_strategy, exploration_strategy(None))\n                .before(exploration_strategy(None))#.before(self.agent.exploration.patrol())\n                .preempt(self.agent, [\n                    exploration_strategy(0).condition(lambda: not diving()),\n                    exploration_strategy(None).until(\n                        self.agent, lambda: self.agent.blstats.hitpoints >= 0.8 * self.agent.blstats.max_hitpoints)\n                ])\n                .preempt(self.agent, [\n                    self.agent.exploration.explore_stairs(go_to_strategy, all=True).condition(explore_stairs_condition),\n                ])\n                .until(self.agent, condition)\n            ).run()\n\n            # hypothesis (see Agent.handle_exception): once the current level is fully explored and\n            # searched, every sub-strategy declines without acting while the milestone condition (e.g.\n            # Xp8 on Dlvl 1) is still unmet, so this loop spins forever without a single game action --\n            # the agent hangs, the game idles until the no-progress timeout and the run's remaining\n            # progress is forfeited. After many consecutive action-less passes, search in place so\n            # game time passes (monsters spawn and come to us, XP keeps growing) instead of hanging.\n            if self.agent.step_count == step_count_before:\n                idle_iterations += 1\n                if idle_iterations >= 20:\n                    idle_iterations = 0\n                    self.agent.search(10)\n            else:\n                idle_iterations = 0\n\n    # hypothesis: gnomes and dwarves (cav/hea/ran-gno, val-dwa) walk the Mines after the Xp 8 grind\n    # among *peaceful* dwarves, so unlike every other race they never kill one for the pick-axe or\n    # mattock ~64% of them carry, and without a digging tool they dive by the stairs and die at\n    # Dlvl 2-10 (the Archeologist, who has a pick, averages Dlvl 17). Deliberately picking a fight\n    # with one peaceful dwarf is cheap: melee angers it before it dies, so there is no Luck\n    # penalty, only a few alignment points, and an Xp 8 character with most of its HP wins the\n    # fight. Once the pick is in the pack the existing machinery (milestone -> GO_DOWN, dig_down\n    # under Elbereth) turns the rest of the game into a dig dive. Only applies after the grind, so\n    # the Dlvl 1 game is byte-identical to the parent's.\n    # From github.com/Komershan/nethacker@d3d40a6.\n    @Strategy.wrap\n    def anger_peaceful_dwarf(self):\n        a = self.agent\n        if a.character.race not in (Character.GNOME, Character.DWARF) or \\\n                self.milestone == Milestone.BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL or \\\n                a.character.prop.hallu or a.character.prop.polymorph or \\\n                a.blstats.hitpoints < 0.8 * a.blstats.max_hitpoints or \\\n                a.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.WEAK or \\\n                a.pick_for_digging() is not None:\n            yield False\n        level = a.current_level()\n        # never where the Watch or a shopkeeper could get involved\n        if (self.minetown_level is not None and level.key() == self.minetown_level) or \\\n                utils.isin(a.glyphs, G.SHOPKEEPER).any() or level.shop[a.blstats.y, a.blstats.x]:\n            yield False\n        peaceful = a.monster_tracker.peaceful_monster_mask\n        dis = a.bfs()\n        best = None\n        for y, x in zip(*peaceful.nonzero()):\n            if not MON.is_monster(a.glyphs[y, x]):\n                continue\n            name = MON.permonst(a.glyphs[y, x]).mname\n            if name.startswith('watch'):\n                yield False\n            if name not in ('dwarf', 'dwarf lord', 'dwarf king'):\n                continue\n            nd = dis[max(y - 1, 0):y + 2, max(x - 1, 0):x + 2]\n            nd = nd[nd != -1]\n            if nd.size == 0:\n                continue\n            d = int(nd.min())\n            if d <= 12 and (best is None or d < best[0]):\n                best = (d, y, x)\n        if best is None:\n            yield False\n        yield True\n        _, y, x = best\n        if utils.adjacent((y, x), (a.blstats.y, a.blstats.x)):\n            a.melee_attack(y, x)\n            # the tracker carries peacefulness over from the previous frame; force a fresh\n            # monster listing so fight2 sees the now hostile dwarf\n            a.monster_tracker.on_panic()\n            return\n        a.go_to(y, x, stop_one_before=True, max_steps=1)\n\n    def global_strategy(self):\n        return (\n            self.current_strategy().repeat()\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.solve_sokoban_strategy()\n                .condition(lambda: self.milestone == Milestone.SOLVE_SOKOBAN and\n                                   self.agent.current_level().dungeon_number == Level.SOKOBAN)\n            ])\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.offer_corpses().preempt(self.agent, [\n                    self.agent.eat_corpses_from_ground().condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY),\n                ]),\n            ])\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.wait_out_unexpected_state_strategy(),\n            ])\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.agent.cure_disease().every(5),\n            ])\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.agent.eat_corpses_from_ground(only_below_me=True).condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY),\n                self.agent.eat_corpses_from_ground().every(5).condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY),\n                self.agent.eat_from_inventory().every(5),\n            ])\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.follow_guard(),\n            ])\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.anger_peaceful_dwarf(),\n            ])\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.agent.fight2(),\n            ])\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.agent.engulfed_fight(),\n            ])\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.agent.proactive_sleep_strategy(),\n            ])\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.agent.emergency_strategy(),\n            ])\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.agent.read_magic_mapping(),\n            ])\n            .preempt(self.agent, [\n                self.agent.dig_down(),\n            ])\n        )","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":921,"totalLines":921,"truncated":false}},"title":"autoascend/global_logic.py","time":{"start":1790527659312,"end":1790527659323}},"id":"prt_0e3c3dd2a001zTE2JU57QxXWny","sessionID":"ses_f1c5a4875ffeR5KO5Iu7pV8EKt","messageID":"msg_0e3c3c1b5001CTK7pICcu3YeRl"}}
