{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790529809924,"sessionID":"ses_f1c5a4875ffeR5KO5Iu7pV8EKt","part":{"id":"prt_0e3e3c4c7001YDhWf35Jue4Nug","messageID":"msg_0e3d853890019n3pLWno3VWy9h","sessionID":"ses_f1c5a4875ffeR5KO5Iu7pV8EKt","type":"reasoning","text":"OK so there are no attempts tried yet. Let me now think about what focused change I should make.\n\nLooking at the data again, the key issues are:\n1. Starvation early (seeds 2, 12, 14)\n2. Early monster deaths to basic threats\n3. The bot stays on Dlvl 1 grinding experience and dies there\n\nThe healer role starts with a spell (healing) and presumably starts with some food. Let me check what the Healer starts with.\n\nActually, I realize I should focus on understanding the root cause of the early deaths. Let me think about what the Healer does at the start:\n\nThe Healer role in NetHack starts with:\n- A scalpel\n- A stethoscope\n- A holy sword (or similar)\n- Some food\n- A potion of healing\n- etc.\n\nA gnome Healer starts with some advantages:\n- Gnomes get intrinsics (poison resistance) at higher XL\n- They can use magic mapping\n\nThe key question: Why do seeds 2, 12, 14 starve at Xp:3-4?\n\nLet me look at the eat_corpses_from_ground and eat_from_inventory strategies:\n\nIn global_logic.py:\n```python\n.preempt(self.agent, [\n    self.agent.eat_corpes_from_ground().condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY),\n    self.agent.eat_corpes_from_ground().every(5).condition(lambda: self.agent.blstats.hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY),\n    self.agent.eat_from_inventory().every(5),\n])\n```\n\nThe eat_corpes_from_ground only triggers when `hunger_state >= Hunger.NOT_HUNGRY`, and then only every 5 turns when still NOT_HUNGRY. The eat_from_inventory triggers every 5 turns.\n\nBut wait, the user asked to make ONE focused change marked with a `# hypothesis: …` comment. The system ... the default is usually 1000 turns or so.\n\nActually, let me look at the inventory code to understand the hunger mechanics better. But first, let me think about what the actual problem is.\n\nLooking at the early deaths:\n- Seed 2: starved at Xp:4 - this means the bot ran out of food before reaching Xp 4 on Dlvl 1\n- Seeds 12, 14: killed by hobbit at Xp:4 - also early\n\nThe Healer starts with a stethoscope and scalpel, and some food. A gnome Healer starts with food. But the bot might not be eating enough.\n\nActually, let me look at the `eat_from_inventory` and `eat_corpes_from_ground` strategies more carefully, and also the `eat_from_inventory` in agent.py.\n\nLet me look at the eat functions in agent.py:","time":{"start":1790529750215,"end":1790529809904}}}
