{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1790529844799,"sessionID":"ses_f1c5a4875ffeR5KO5Iu7pV8EKt","part":{"id":"prt_0e3e5363b00110QZAVtf54j0U0","messageID":"msg_0e3e533cf001T1aaQkKbaJQxCR","sessionID":"ses_f1c5a4875ffeR5KO5Iu7pV8EKt","snapshot":"44f8accb8718e4d74878d45e7ccf1a8a5d818306","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790529883605,"sessionID":"ses_f1c5a4875ffeR5KO5Iu7pV8EKt","part":{"id":"prt_0e3e5363d001sJRwRC4owMFDrI","messageID":"msg_0e3e533cf001T1aaQkKbaJQxCR","sessionID":"ses_f1c5a4875ffeR5KO5Iu7pV8EKt","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I understand the corpse eating logic. The key issue for the Healer gnome:\n\nFor a gnome, `_is_corpse_editable` doesn't return False for poison or acid (since `self.character.race != Character.ORC` is True for gnome, so the check `self.character.race != Character.ORC` is True, meaning it WILL return False for poison... wait let me re-read:\n\n```python\nif self.character.race != Character.ORC and permonst.mflags1 & MON.M1_POIS != 0:\n    return False\n```\n\nFor a gnome, `self.character.race != Character.ORC` is True (gnome != orc), so if the monster has M1_POIS flag, it returns False. This means gnomes can't eat poisonous corpses. That's fine.\n\nBut the bigger issue is that the bot may not be finding or eating corpses early enough.\n\nLet me now think about the key hypothesis for improvement.\n\nLooking at the data, the biggest losses are:\n1. Starvation early (3 seeds)\n2. Death to basic monsters (many seeds)\n\nThe bot's global strategy has these preemptive layers:\n1. current_strategy() (milestone-based)\n2. Sokoban\n3. Offer corpses + eat from ground\n4. Wait unexpected state\n5. Cure disease\n6. Eat from ground + eat from inventory\n7. Follow guard\n8. Anger peaceful dwarf\n9. Fight2\n10. Engulfed fight\n11. Proactive sleep\n12. Emergency strategy\n13. Read magic mapping\n14. Dig down\n\nThe problem is that on Dlvl 1, the bot grinds to Xp 8 and then tries to find the Gnomish Mines. But before reaching Xp 8 or the mines, it dies to monsters or starves.\n\nLet me think about what a focused improvement would be. The key insight from the data:\n\n- Seed 8 scores 0.554 by reaching Dlvl:27 - this is the \"deep dive\" seed that finds a digging wand and dives deep\n- Most other seeds stall at Xp:3-9 on Dlvl:1-2 and die\n\nThe key improvement would be to help the bot survive the early game better, so more seeds reach the deep phase where they can score well.\n\nKey ideas:\n1. **Engrave Elbereth earlier** - This is the most important early-game survival tactic. Engraving \"Elbereth\" on the floor makes monsters afraid to approach.\n2. **Better food management** - Eat more frequently, especially early game\n3. **Avoid unnecessary early fights** - Use conflict or other tactics\n4. **Start diving earlier** - Once at Xp 5+, dig down if you have a pick\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the global_strategy more carefully. The `current_strategy()` milestone system has this flow:\n\n1. BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL - grind to Xp 8 (or leave when hungry for certain roles)\n2. Then transition to FIND_GNOMISH_MINES or GO_DOWN\n\nThe condition for leaving BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL for non-gnome, non-dwarf roles:\n```python\nif self.milestone == Milestone.BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL and race != Character.GNOME and \\\n    not mines_folk:\n    if PICK_HUNT_TURNS > 0 and self._role_routes() and race != Character.DWARF:\n        self._pick_hunt_start = self.agent.blstats.time\n        self.milestone = Milestone.FIND_GNOMISH_MINES\n    else:\n        self.milestone = Milestone.GO_DOWN\n    continue\n```\n\nFor a Healer gnome (`hea-gno-neu-mal`): race=GNOME, so `race != Character.GNOME` is False, so this whole block is skipped. The bot stays in BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL until Xp >= _grind_xl() = 8 (for Healer, ROLE_GRIND_XL defaults to GRIND_XL = 8) OR until LEAVE_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY conditions are met.\n\nBut Healer is NOT in ROLES_LEAVING_GRIND_WHEN_HUNGRY, so the bot stays grinding to Xp 8 on Dlvl 1.\n\nThe problem: The bot starts on Dlvl 1 with limited food. Grinding to Xp 8 takes many turns, and the bot may starve before reaching Xp 8. Also, even if it reaches Xp 8, it may die to monsters before it can transition out of BE_ON_FIRST_LEVEL or find the mines.\n\nLet me think about the best focused change...\n\nActually, I realize the most impactful change would be to add Elbereth engraving early in the game. Elbereth (engraving \"Elbereth\" on the floor) is the single most effective early-game survival tactic in NetHack - it causes most monsters to avoid the player.\n\nBut the current code does have `elbereth_action` in `fight2()`, which checks if the player has already engraved Elbereth. The issue is that the bot may not be engraving Elbereth early enough.\n\nWait, let me look at the elbereth_action function more carefully:\n\n```python\ndef elbereth_action(agent, monsters):\n    if agent.inventory.engraving_below_me.lower() == 'elbereth':\n        return []\n    if not agent.can_engrave():\n        return []\n    ...\n    if agent.blstats.hitpoints < 30 and adj_monsters_count > 0:\n        return [(-15 + 20 * adj_monster\n```\n\nSo elbereth_action only returns actions when the player is below 30 HP and adjacent to monsters. It doesn't proactively engrave Elbereth at the start of the game.\n\nThe key hypothesis: **If the bot proactively engraves Elbereth early in the game (when first arriving on Dlvl 1, or as one of the first actions), many early deaths would be prevented, allowing more seeds to reach deeper levels.**\n\nBut wait - engraving takes time and resources. Let me think about another approach.\n\nActually, let me re-read the problem statement more carefully:\n\n> Make ONE focused change, marked with a `# hypothesis: …` comment saying what you expect it to improve.\n\nThe change should be in the strategy code in the `autoascend/` package.\n\nLet me think about what change would have the most impact. Based on my analysis:\n\n1. The bot dies to basic monsters early because it doesn't engrave Elbereth\n2. The bot starves because it doesn't eat often enough\n3. The bot stays on Dlvl 1 grinding and doesn't dive\n\nThe most focused and impactful change would be to add early Elbereth engraving. Let me look at how and where to add this.\n\nActually, looking at the code flow again, I notice that the `wait_out_unexpected_state_strategy` is in the global strategy preemptions, but there's no explicit Elbereth engraving strategy.\n\nLet me look at what the `can_engrave` function does and how engraving works:","time":{"start":1790529844797,"end":1790529883587}}}
